d defaults and no proven agent-specific injection. | **Worth investigating, not ready to add.** Editor identity or `CONTINUE_CLI_BASH_*` configuration is not a reliable execution signal. |\n| SWE-agent (`SWE-agent/SWE-agent`) | 20,672 stars; pushed 2026-10-26; release `v1.1.0` (`0f3acafacabc0def8cc76b4e48acb4b6cf302cb9`) [D5] | Runs commands in SWE-ReX deployments/shell sessions. | Reviewed release environment orchestration did not expose a stable agent-specific variable to command children. Container/runtime identity would be too broad. | **Worth investigating, not ready to add.** Seek a SWE-ReX/SWE-agent explicit child contract. |\n| Amazon Q Developer CLI (`aws/amazon-q-developer-cli`) | 1,984 stars; pushed 2026-08-24; release `v1.19.7` (`cf39ab6297ee7654fcbeed253445d35fe5c92b07`) [D2] | Agent Execute tool constructs the complete command environment. | It appends `AmazonQ-For-CLI Version/<version>` to `AWS_EXECUTION_ENV` and passes that environment to commands. The variable is shared across AWS products, so presence alone is unsafe. | **Worth a value-aware rule, not ready for the current rule types.** A contains/token contract and collision tests are needed; never detect `AWS_EXECUTION_ENV` by presence. |\n\n## 5. Follow-up work\n\n| Priority | Evidence-backed action | Uncertainty / focused tests |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | Remove `ZED_TERM` and `ZED_ENVIRONMENT` as agent signals, or replace them only if Zed publishes an agent-specific child contract [U8][U9]. | Validate ordinary local, remote, CLI-opened, and worktree-shell paths with mocked environment tests; no live claim is made here. |\n| P0 | Remove `GOOSE_PROVIDER` from agent detection [U10]. | Add a regression showing provider configuration alone remains non-LLM. Continue researching `GOOSE_TERMINAL`; current evidence is incomplete. |\n| P1 | Add Pi detection using non-empty `PI_SESSION_ID` [D4]. | Cover default child injection, `exposeSessionEnvironment=false`, empty value, inherited-value deletion, and nested harness accumulation. |\n| P1 | Ask Amazon Q to document a stable child attribution contract, then add value-aware matching only if the `AmazonQ-For-CLI` token remains contractual [D2]. | Existing exact-value rules cannot safely match version-bearing/appended values. Presence would be a broad AWS false positive. |\n| P1 | Correct the Copilot app comment that says precedence: implementation accumulates labels. | Add app+VS Code and CLI+app overlap tests, plus exact output order. |\n| P2 | Add empty, whitespace, wrong-value, mixed-case, same-label-multi-alternative, and all-label ordering tests [S2][S6]. | Decide explicitly whether whitespace should count as present. Preserve current behavior unless intentionally changed. |\n| P2 | Request public child-process contracts from closed-source vendors and for `OR_APP_NAME`, credentials, home directories, trace IDs, workspace IDs, and generic flags. | Do not remove unverified signals solely because searches found no evidence; absence from search is not removal proof. |\n\n## 6. Limitations\n\n- This was source-only. No signal was runtime-tested. SDK mocked tests establish mapping semantics, not upstream behavior.\n- GitHub code search returned HTTP 429 and its one permitted retry was denied by the non-interactive environment; code search was stopped as required. Repository trees and targeted contents API reads were used instead.\n- A dedicated `web-fetch` capability was unavailable, so vendor documentation outside public GitHub repositories could not be read. This especially limits closed-source Cursor, Copilot app, Amp, Windsurf, Replit, Augment, and Antigravity assessment.\n- Public repositories for Claude Code and Copilot CLI expose releases/docs but not the relevant implementation. Factory/Droid exposes docs; Cursor and Windsurf repositories do not expose current product source.\n- Codex `CODEX_SANDBOX` verification is specific to macOS Seatbelt. Other operating systems, remote execution, exec-server paths, inherited environment policies, and user overrides remain partially reviewed.\n- Gemini and Qwen evidence covers current subprocess and PTY paths. VS Code evidence covers Copilot-created terminals and the documented all-agent-process contract.\n- Unreviewed or unresolved alternatives are exactly the 32 rows marked Unverifiable; none is silently omitted.\n- Retrieval stayed below the 150-request ceiling. Four discovery searches were used; one GitHub code-search request plus one failed retry were used, below the six-search and ten-code-search limits.\n- Discovery search precision was imperfect: recently updated results contained many extensions/wrappers. Candidate selection therefore required official ownership, command execution relevance, adoption/activity, and non-archived status.\n\n## 7. Sources\n\nAll sources accessed 2026-10-29 UTC. Excerpts are short and line ranges are the relevant release windows.\n\n- [S1](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/blob/7d24d6cf305b1d175811c32490bdd3d543ad51c1/src/Cli/dotnet/Telemetry/LLMEnvironmentDetectorForTelemetry.cs#L10-L96): complete 25-label detector; `Select`/`Where` then `string.Join` accumulates all matches.\n- [S2](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/blob/7d24d6cf305b1d175811c32490bdd3d543ad51c1/src/Cli/Microsoft.DotNet.Cli.Definitions/Telemetry/EnvironmentDetectionRule.cs#L54-L143): presence is `!string.IsNullOrEmpty`; values use `OrdinalIgnoreCase`.\n- [S3](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/blob/7d24d6cf305b1d175811c32490bdd3d543ad51c1/src/Cli/dotnet/Telemetry/TelemetryCommonProperties.cs#L45-L70): telemetry property key `llm`.\n- [S4](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/blob/7d24d6cf305b1d175811c32490bdd3d543ad51c1/src/Cli/dotnet/Commands/Run/CommonRunHelpers.cs#L113-L128): LLM detection adds Terminal Logger disable-node-display argument.\n- [S5](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/blob/7d24d6cf305b1d175811c32490bdd3d543ad51c1/src/Cli/dotnet/Commands/Test/MTP/MicrosoftTestingPlatformTestCommand.cs#L1168-L1186): LLM detection selects `AnsiMode.NoAnsi`,